  "title": "About Livecode Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "bb6d3678f2754a6c",
      "text": "The Livecode plugin runs a Livecode wasm stack as a wiki widget. A `livecode` item loads and displays its stack by default; add `BOOT click` for a collapsible poster card that boots on demand. Every widget runs independently — the stop control collapses a running widget back to its poster, and a watchdog tears a frame down when its item leaves the lineup."
    },
    {
      "type": "livecode",
      "id": "3b8ba788403d6699",
      "text": "STACK https://wasm.livecode.wiki/assets/wasm/shared/stack.html?zip=hexagon.zip\nTITLE Hexagon\nHEIGHT 460"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4b7e9d2c8f0a3615",
      "text": "# Commands\nUPPERCASE first word, optional colon, one per line:\n\n- STACK — the standalone's shell page: absolute `https://...` or a path relative to the item's origin site\n- TITLE — the poster label; defaults to the shell file name\n- HEIGHT — iframe height in pixels; defaults to 420\n- BOOT — `auto` (default) loads and displays on render; `click` shows a collapsible poster instead\n- FULLSCREEN — `fixed` (default), `scale`, or `resize`; how the stack behaves when the full control is used — see [[Full Screen Wasm]]\n- NAME — the stack's name, needed only by `resize` mode for the JavaScript bridge call"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "e5b09c3a71d8f246",
      "text": "# Script only stacks\nAn item whose text is a script only stack — beginning `script \"Name\"` — boots that script directly: the shell builds the standalone payload in the browser from the item text, so no export is needed. Command lines above the script line still apply, and the stack's name becomes the widget's NAME for the JavaScript bridge. For now the script runs aboard a small host stack, until a blank host is exported. Live:"
    },
    {
      "type": "livecode",
      "id": "9c2e6f80b5a3d417",
      "text": "script \"Simple Test\"\non openstack\n   create button \"Hello World\"\nend openstack"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "5c8f0a1d9e2b4736",
      "text": "# Design\nDoor two of [[Three Livecode Doors]]: one shared engine pair per Livecode version is cached by the browser, so many widgets cost one engine download plus a small `standalone.zip` each. Messages the stack posts surface as a `livecodeMessage` event on the widget — the grounding for the [[WikiScript]] stage dialect. See [[Livecode Wasm]] for the export anatomy and the trimmed shell, and [[Livecode Wasm Windows]] for the script boot design."
    }
  ],
